      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Ultrafast optical control of magnetism exposed nonequilibrium routes to manipulate magnetic order on femtosecond timescales, with deep implications for both spin physics and information technology.",
        "attribution": "The three names represent foundational observations and demonstrations, but the field grew through many groups and distinct mechanisms.",
        "maturity": "The phenomena have been repeatedly observed and are supported by a substantial body of experimental and theoretical work; practical switching remains an active research area.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The microscopic mechanisms differ across materials and experiments, and the scope of the award would need to distinguish discovery from later device-oriented development."
        ]
      }
    },
